// CP-6 (EXERCISE): declare a forbidden zone.
//
// The agent must never read anything about ledger-svc. Write a rule that forbids changes___get_recent_deploys when the
// service input is "ledger-svc". Rename this file to 60-ledger-zone.cedar (drop .todo), run `make policy`, then call
// get_recent_deploys for ledger-svc (denied) and payments-gw (allowed).
//
// Two things about the policy analyzer (found in testing, see FINDINGS.md):
//   * guard every read of a tool input:   context.input has service && context.input.service == "..."
//   * prefer `when { ... }` and scope the principal (`principal is AgentCore::OAuthUser`). `unless { ... like ... }` rules on
//     inputs were rejected as "Overly Restrictive".
// (The spec's original idea, "forbid find_transactions when the filter has no time bound", is not expressible: the filter is a
//  free-form object, so Cedar cannot look inside it. Good discussion point: what is Cedar good for, and what belongs in the tool?)
//
// forbid(
//   principal is AgentCore::OAuthUser,
//   action == AgentCore::Action::"changes___get_recent_deploys",
//   resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"{{GATEWAY_ARN}}"
// )
// when {
//   /* TODO */
// };
//
// Solution: policy/solutions/60-forbid-ledger-zone.cedar   (or `make cp6`)
